# ntfsplus out-of-tree module — pinned source for the generic kmod builder.
# Consumed by build_files/kmods/build-kmods.sh (sourced, not executed).
#
# NTFSPLUS (Namjae Jeon, author of exFAT and ksmbd) is Linux 7.1's in-tree
# fs/ntfs/ — a from-scratch read/write NTFS driver on iomap + folios, coexisting
# with ntfs3 (fs/ntfs3/Kconfig: `depends on !NTFS_FS || m`). The ogc kernel
# builds it off (`# CONFIG_NTFS_FS is not set`), so the image carries no ntfs.ko.
# This is the author's own standalone packaging of that same code, which builds
# out-of-tree from 6.1 upwards.
URL=https://github.com/namjaejeon/linux-ntfs.git
# Pinned commit on main: the 2026-08-30 merge of ntfs-next (PR #83, 60
# commits), which carries "iomap: consolidate bio submission" (upstream PR
# #78) — without it the module NULL-dereferences a bio on the first mount
# under a 7.2 kernel while build-time vermagic checks pass (gotcha #35). The
# previous pin (5685d5b7, ntfs-next merge of wof-v4, 2026-08-25) is an
# ancestor of this one. Bumps follow main merge commits; skip ntfs-next tips —
# the branch is force-pushed and its newest series may be mid-rework (the
# non-compiling 2026-08-27 batch survives only as old_ntfs-next). Every bump
# needs the runtime mount proof of gotcha #35 on a booted target kernel.
COMMIT=8e679ed13f9b300df0488b977d614d7e9bfd05df
# Built object base name: the Makefile emits ntfs.ko and the driver registers the
# filesystem type "ntfs" (MODULE_ALIAS_FS("ntfs")) — the name "ntfsplus" is the
# project's, never the module's nor the mount type's.
KO_NAME=ntfs
# The kbuild fragment is gated on the kernel's own symbol: `obj-$(CONFIG_NTFS_FS)
# += ntfs.o` expands to `obj- += ntfs.o` against a kernel that leaves it unset, so
# kbuild compiles NOTHING and still exits 0 (gotcha #25). Forcing the symbol on the
# make command line is what makes the module build at all.
KO_BUILD_ARGS=CONFIG_NTFS_FS=m
# Destination subpath under /usr/lib/modules/<kver>/ — mirrors the in-tree layout
# (kernel/fs/ntfs) so if a future ogc build enables CONFIG_NTFS_FS, depmod's
# updates/ priority keeps this copy winning.
KO_DEST=updates/fs/ntfs
